he screenshot, \"LIFE\" text at top right and hearts below at y~50.\n\nLet me use write_nametable? No. Let me read the nametable region for the heart row to see the tile IDs, and compare across states. That would be precise. The heart row is at screen y≈48-55 → tile row 6 (y=48-55). x from ~208 to ~248 → tile cols 26-31.\n\nLet me read_nametable x=26,y=6,width=6,height=1.\n\nActually the HUD in the screenshot: hearts at y~50, so tile row 6. Let me read.\n\nLet me do that for the current state (0x066F=48) and for the clean state. Actually, comparing tile IDs tells how many full/empty hearts.\n\nLet me read nametable now."}
