a pixel scan. I'll call get_pixel_color for several points.\n\nHmm, this is a lot of calls. Let me instead read the nametable for BOTH states (0x10 and 0x22) and compare. That's cheap and definitive for tile identity.\n\nCurrent state = 0x22. Let me read nametable rows 5-7, cols 26-31.\n\nActually I already have the 0x30 read. Let me get the 0x10 and 0x22 reads. But the tiles may be identical in all states if the fill difference is via tile... they must differ.\n\nWait, in the 0x30 read, all hearts were tile 36. If in 0x10 state some hearts are also tile 36, then tile doesn't distinguish. Let me check by reading now (0x22).\n\nLet me read nametable x=24,y=6,w=8,h=2."}
