earts (containers and how full they are)\". A reasonable answer: hearts/life is at 0x066F; encoding: high nibble = number of heart containers minus 1; low nibble = number of full hearts minus 1. And the container count may also be reflected at 0x0650 (the max) — let me test.\n\nLet me test 0x0650: restore slot2, write 0x0650=0x32 (50), step, read heart row.\n\nHmm, wait: slot 2 was saved from slot 1 state which was the enemy screen with clean values. Fine.\n\nActually, hold on: I saved slot 2 while paused at the enemy screen with 0x066F=34 (clean) — yes, before any heart writes? Let me check: I saved slot 2 right after the \"all three counters X4\" screenshot? No — I saved slot 2 BEFORE writing 0x0652-0x066E (the first range test). At that time 0x066F was 34 (I had restored slot 0 earlier and then... hmm, actually I had written 0x066F=48,16,34 earlier, then reloaded slot 0 which restored clean, then walked right, then saved slot 2? No.\n\nLet me trace: slot 0 saved at clean start. Then wrote 0x066F=3,48, then load slot 0 (clean). Then read, then wrote 0x066F=16, step, screenshot. Then wrote 0x066F=48, step, read nametable, screenshot. Then wrote 33, read. Then I called load_state slot 0 again and played right 200, then watch 600, screenshot. Then pause, save_state slot 1, wrote 0x066F=16, read tiles, wrote 0x066F=34, read, ... then wrote 16, then 48, then 33, then load_state slot 2? \n\nHmm, actually I saved slot 2 AFTER the heart tests: \"save_state slot 2\" came right after the heart mapping tests (after I'd written 0x066F=33). Let me check: yes, the save_state slot 2 call happened right before the first counter range write. At that moment 0x066F was 33 (from the 0x21 test) or 34? The sequence: wrote 33, read (F2 F2 66), then \"save_state slot 2\", then wrote 0x0652-0x066E = 4 (which doesn't include 0x066F). So 0x066F at slot 2 = 33! Hmm, that means slot 2 has hearts at 2 full.\n\nWait no: after writing 33 and reading, I then did the counter bisection using load_s