olid. Two enclosed areas. Definitely \"8\".\n\nAnd the rupee \"4\" tile (nm 4) — let me read it. If nm 4 = \"4\", then the font at nm 4 is \"4\". And nm 10 = \"8\"? So font tiles: nm0=\"0\", nm4=\"4\", nm10=\"8\"? Let me check nm 9 = \"5\". Hmm, so the font might be: nm 0=\"0\", 1=\"1\", ..., but nm9=\"5\"? That breaks.\n\nUnless the font is: nm 0=\"0\", nm1=\"1\", nm2=\"2\", nm3=\"3\", nm4=\"4\", nm5=\"5\", nm6=\"6\"","truncated":true}
